# The install scripts have exactly ONE copy, in the product repository. This
# file makes rookery.cloud serve them by redirecting to it, rather than
# vendoring copies here that would silently drift — the same failure the
# brand-logo manifest already has to be defended against.
#
# These MUST be real HTTP redirects, not Astro's `redirects:` config. That
# emits an HTML page carrying <meta http-equiv="refresh">, which a browser
# follows and `curl -fsSL` does not — so the advertised
# `curl -fsSL https://rookery.sh/install.sh | sh` would pipe an HTML document
# into a shell. curl and PowerShell's `irm` both follow a 302.
#
# This site is hosted on Cloudflare Workers, which parses this file natively.
# There is deliberately no `!` force suffix: Workers rejects it and fails the
# entire deploy. The suffix was never buying anything here anyway — it forces
# a rule ahead of static-file matching, and neither /install.sh nor
# /install.ps1 has a file here to lose to.
#
# Both 404 until the product repository is public: raw.githubusercontent.com
# needs an authenticated request for a private repo. That is a release step, and
# no redirect can fix it.
/install.sh   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rookery-ai/rookery/main/install.sh   302
/install.ps1  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rookery-ai/rookery/main/install.ps1  302

# Astro/Starlight emits no /docs/index.html — only leaf pages exist — but the
# product repository's README advertises "Documentation -> rookery.cloud/docs"
# as a bare URL. Without this, that advertised link 404s. Redirect to the
# first page in the documentation sidebar rather than Astro's `redirects:`
# config, for the same reason /install.sh above uses a real HTTP redirect:
# that config emits a <meta http-equiv="refresh"> page that curl does not
# follow. These match /docs and /docs/ exactly (no trailing splat), so they
# cannot swallow /docs/anything and redirect the rest of the documentation
# tree along with it.
/docs   /docs/getting-started/what-rookery-is/   302
/docs/  /docs/getting-started/what-rookery-is/   302
